"name"},{"s":"fact","w":"4"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A fridge cut open in the middle of a kitchen: it starts as an icebox (food and a block of ice), the ice melts, a frosting coil replaces it, the coil runs out, and a compressor with coils underneath closes the loop. The camera opens close on the ice and the food, stays mid on the fridge and its parts for the chain, and ends on the home view with the compressor humming and the door open.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you put food in a box with ice, you have a fridge."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the ice melts and drips onto the food."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a coil of liquid that boils at minus 26 degrees, and it frosts."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But the coil's liquid boils away, the frost melts and the box warms."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a compressor that squeezes the gas back into a liquid."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a refrigerator."},{"role":"how","text":"Squeezing makes the gas hot, so coils underneath shed that heat."},{"role":"fact","text":"It holds your food at 4 degrees Celsius."},{"role":"myth","text":"And the cold is not blown in."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"A fridge only moves heat out to the coils outside."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a glass door, shelves and a light."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a fridge."}]}